From 02b0e36ec881b96c387d0c134673b89236005f05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Mausberg <samuelmausberg@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 03:23:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] hostgap: sync-free FlashInfer plan for the DFlash draft
 forward

The DFlash draft forward runs in TARGET_VERIFY mode over the drafter's
sliding-window and full-attention layers. With two wrappers it cannot take
fast_prefill_plan, so every cycle plain plan() reads qo_indptr,
paged_kv_indptr and last_page_len back from the device for each wrapper:
six blocking reads that wait for the previous verify and draft extend.

The worker now records the exact host copy of the draft forward's device
seq_lens (batch.seq_lens_cpu, non-compact path only). With
SGLANG_HOSTGAP_DFLASH_DRAFT_PLAN=1 the two wrappers plan on replays with
fast_verify_plan from that copy: min(seq_len, window) for the
sliding-window wrapper and seq_len for the full one, plus the block, with
CUDA-graph padding rows taken from the padded host mirror. Without the
host copy the stock plan() runs. SGLANG_HOSTGAP_VALIDATE=1 checks every
such plan against the stock path. Off by default.
